From: unjordi <jordi.serra@pind.mx>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: host-common: keep the root-port D3cold veto for suspend-to-RAM

Letting only endpoints veto D3cold powers the Qualcomm PCIe controller off
during PSCI system suspend too. With the controller off,
qcom_pcie_set_suspend_opp() drops its interconnect vote for
PM_SUSPEND_MEM, nothing keeps a DDR vote, and an SM8550 (Retroid Pocket 6)
never resumes from deep: 3/3 hangs at "PM: suspend entry (deep)", and a
reset ~90 s after an RTC wake.

Keep the endpoint-only rule for s2idle, where the opp-suspend floor holds
DDR, and restore the root-port veto for suspend-to-RAM. Measured on the RP6:
deep suspend + RTC wake returns with this behaviour (endpoint_d3cold=0
equivalent), both with a raw write to /sys/power/state and through
systemctl suspend.
---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <linux/of_pci.h>
 #include <linux/pci-ecam.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 
 #include "pci-host-common.h"
 
@@ -296,7 +297,11 @@
 	if (!pdev->dev.driver && !pci_is_enabled(pdev))
 		return 0;
 
-	if (endpoint_d3cold) {
+	/*
+	 * Not for suspend-to-RAM: once the controller powers off, nothing keeps a
+	 * DDR vote through PSCI system suspend and SM8550 never returns from it.
+	 */
+	if (endpoint_d3cold && pm_suspend_target_state != PM_SUSPEND_MEM) {
 		switch (pci_pcie_type(pdev)) {
 		case PCI_EXP_TYPE_ENDPOINT:
 		case PCI_EXP_TYPE_LEG_END:
